From: Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:29:19 +0200
Subject: Fix GHSA-mmf9-xm3v-hg2x: quadratic folded header concatenation

Each folded response header line was concatenated with the whole
accumulated header value into a newly allocated string. That made
parsing of a header split into many continuation lines quadratic, so a
malicious server could stall the client for a long time with a few MB
of headers.

Accumulate the last header line in a smart_str instead so folding is
linear in the total header size.

(cherry picked from commit a303f697268d42f6671c9d4c479ff90bbf301db1)
(cherry picked from commit e371eee5ce835619e52fb9acbed9f79f1235d853)
(cherry picked from commit ff9a660811d1dfc1062ef9dc1e6cd1ba8047e11b)
(cherry picked from commit ed1de09f6bd108d32e21417dbe9ac1bea232d6d3)
(cherry picked from commit 6422895cf27c7501a676ef9a72257a766911c196)
---
